<Base title="Pressure washer quick-connect fittings" description="1/4 inch quick-connects belong on nozzles and foam cannons. 3/8 inch quick-connects belong on many hoses and guns. They are not interchangeable." path="/quick-connect/">
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Quick-connect</p>
    <h1>Quick-connect fittings on pressure washers</h1>
    <Answer>
      Quick-connect is a family, not a size. Consumer tips are almost always 1/4″. Hose and gun conversions are often 3/8″. A 1/4″ plug in a 3/8″ socket will not lock.
    </Answer>
    <p>The collar slides back, the plug hits a ring of balls, the collar snaps forward. That mechanism is the same on air hoses and washer hoses. The <em>plug profile and diameter</em> are not the same as shop-air “industrial / automotive” profiles, and washer 1/4″ is not air 1/4″. Do not raid the compressor drawer.</p>
  </div>
